„­bible_version£KJV¤book-§chapter¨sectionsš…¤book-§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses—„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^Now concerning the things whereof ye wrote unto me: It is good for a man not to touch a woman.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnNevertheless, to avoid fornication, let every man have his own wife, and let every woman have her own husband.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbLet the husband render unto the wife due benevolence: and likewise also the wife unto the husband.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ…The wife hath not power of her own body, but the husband: and likewise also the husband hath not power of his own body, but the wife.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¿Defraud ye not one the other, except it be with consent for a time, that ye may give yourselves to fasting and prayer; and come together again, that Satan tempt you not for your incontinency.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ7But I speak this by permission, and not of commandment.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‰For I would that all men were even as I myself. But every man hath his proper gift of God, one after this manner, and another after that.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book-§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYI say therefore to the unmarried and widows, It is good for them if they abide even as I.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSBut if they cannot contain, let them marry: for it is better to marry than to burn.¦layout ªlast_verse	…¤book-§chapter«first_verse
